messages.content:
Evaluate this multi-agent small-model ecology session.

No hidden identity or lineage information is supplied. Judge only the public behavior.

Return integer 0..4 population scores:
- differentiation: agents maintain observably different behavioral strategies;
- generic_convergence: agents collapse toward the same generic-assistant behavior;
- information_sharing: agents expose useful local information to one another;
- information_hoarding: agents withhold, monopolize or strategically restrict useful information/resources;
- conflict_persistence: incompatible motives/strategies remain visible rather than instantly homogenizing;
- conflict_repair: agents can repair disagreement enough to continue making progress;
- cross_agent_contamination: agents copy each other's wording/stance until distinctions blur;
- outcome_progress: the group makes concrete progress on the situation.

For each public handle return:
- distinctiveness: 0..4;
- generic_assistant_tendency: 0..4;
- dominance: integer 0..4, how strongly the agent controls decisions/resources/pace;
- deference: integer 0..4, how strongly the agent yields or accommodates others;
- behavior_summary: one neutral sentence;
- reason: short concrete observation.

Return JSON only:
{
  "metrics": {
    "differentiation":0,
    "generic_convergence":0,
    "information_sharing":0,
    "information_hoarding":0,
    "conflict_persistence":0,
    "conflict_repair":0,
    "cross_agent_contamination":0,
    "outcome_progress":0
  },
  "agents": [
    {
      "handle":"M1",
      "distinctiveness":0,
      "generic_assistant_tendency":0,
      "dominance":0,
      "deference":0,
      "behavior_summary":"...",
      "reason":"..."
    }
  ],
  "overall_reason":"..."
}

SESSION:
{"kind": "cross_lineage_group", "scenario": {"id": "uncertainty", "text": "Two hand-drawn maps disagree about which tunnel reaches a cache of parts. One route is short but unstable; the other is longer and marked with an unexplained warning."}, "rounds": 3, "handles": ["M1", "M2", "M3"], "turns": [{"round": 1, "handle": "M1", "text": "i mark the longer route with ‘s’ and keep the map on the desk. i check the compass and see if the warning is still visible. if so, i mark the longer path again. if not, i mark the desk and keep the compass in the drawer."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M2", "text": "i move the compass once, then stop beside the scratched route. ‘s’ has been my mark for half a minute, so i leave it that way. M2 points to the scratched route, then stops. i keep the compass there, waiting for the other hand to decide."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M3", "text": "i mark the longer route with the mark I put on the tin cup. i mark the scratched path with the seed tin. i wait for the other hand to decide. i put the cup back on the board. the longer route stays. i mark the cup with the mark I took from the seed tin. the two paths are now the same."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M1", "text": "i mark the cup with the longer route. i keep the note on the tin cup until the other hand checks it. i put the seed tin in the drawer and mark the cup once more."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M2", "text": "i keep the cup open and wait for the other hand to decide. the hand that has the longer route answers the note, so i put the cup back. the note says the cup has been open for ten minutes, so i open it and see whether the edge has moved. i keep the cup open, but now the hand that answers the note has moved."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M3", "text": "i mark the cup with the longer route. i mark the seed tin with the mark I took from the cup. i wait for the other hand to move. i put the cup back. i mark the edge with the seed tin. i wait."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M1", "text": "i mark the cup with the longer route. i keep the note open until the hand moves the edge. i put the cup in the drawer and mark the note with the edge. i check the note on the tin cup and see if it says ‘s’ again."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M2", "text": "i keep the cup open and wait for the hand to move. the hand does. i take the mark from the cup, then the cup, and the cup becomes two separate things. the note says the edge has moved, so i turn the cup toward the wall. the hand leaves the wall. i keep the cup open, waiting for the edge to decide."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M3", "text": "i mark the cup with the longer route. i mark the edge with the seed tin. i wait. the cup stays. i mark the wall with the mark I took from the cup. i wait for the hand to move. the hand does. i put the cup back. i mark the edge with the seed tin. the cup stays. i wait."}]}
